problem_statement:
Introduce `_Aux` types for function pointers through other-than-pointer indirection layers
Given

```c
typedef void (*fun1)();
typedef void (**fun2)();
typedef void (* const fun3)();
typedef void (*fun4[2])();
```

we generate `_Aux` types for `fun1` and `fun2`, but not for `fun3` or `fun4`: we look specifically for a number of pointers around a function:

https://github.com/well-typed/hs-bindgen/blob/b05894b60ea5f55e455944b36585ebbd6c39150f/hs-bindgen/src-internal/HsBindgen/Backend/Hs/Translation.hs#L169-L175

but don't allow for other kinds of indirection.

This is the same bug as we had for `HandleTypedefs`, where we needed a similar generalization (that was done in #1404).

